METIS END USER LICENCE AGREEMENT

Copyright (c) 2026 Metis. All rights reserved.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DRAFT — NOT YET REVIEWED BY A LAWYER

This agreement was drafted from standard templates and has not been reviewed by
a qualified legal professional. It is a starting point, not legal advice. Metis
captures the screen of the computer it runs on and sends it to a third-party AI
provider, which means it processes information belonging to people who are not
its user — anyone whose message, document or face happens to be on that screen.
That is the part of this product most likely to attract a legal obligation, and
it should be looked at by a lawyer familiar with the data protection law of the
places Metis is distributed before this software is offered publicly.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This End User Licence Agreement ("Agreement") is a legal agreement between you
("You") and Metis ("Licensor") for the Metis software, including its
executables, installers, documentation and any updates ("the Software").

BY INSTALLING, COPYING OR USING THE SOFTWARE YOU AGREE TO BE BOUND BY THIS
AGREEMENT. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE, DO NOT INSTALL OR USE THE SOFTWARE.


1. LICENCE GRANTED

Licensor grants You a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable
licence to install and use the Software on computers You own or control, for
Your own purposes. No other rights are granted.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

You may not:

  (a) sell, rent, lease, sublicense, distribute or otherwise make the Software
      available to anyone else;
  (b) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except to the
      extent that applicable law expressly permits it despite this limitation;
  (c) remove or alter any copyright, trade mark or other proprietary notice;
  (d) use the Software to capture, process or transmit information you do not
      have the right to capture, process or transmit; or
  (e) use the Software in any way that breaks the law where You are.

Publication of the Software's source code, if any, does not grant any licence
beyond this Agreement. The Software is source-available, not open source.


3. YOUR OWN AI PROVIDER ACCOUNTS

The Software works by sending Your requests — which may include a picture of
Your screen, a recording of Your voice, and a list of the controls on Your
screen — to an artificial intelligence provider that You choose and configure,
using credentials that You supply.

You are the customer of that provider, not Licensor. You are responsible for
Your account with them, for any charges it incurs, and for complying with their
terms of service and acceptable use policies. Licensor is not a party to that
relationship and has no control over what those providers do with what You send
them.


4. YOUR RESPONSIBILITY FOR WHAT IS ON YOUR SCREEN

The Software captures the whole of Your desktop. That capture may include
information belonging to other people.

You are responsible for ensuring You have the right to capture and transmit
whatever is on Your screen when You use the Software, including any personal
data of others, confidential information, or material subject to an obligation
of secrecy. The Software provides controls for withholding parts of the screen,
and it honours the flag Windows applications use to mark their own content as
not to be captured, but these are aids and not a guarantee. Where You are
uncertain, do not use the Software on that screen.


5. AUTONOMOUS AGENTS

The Software includes an optional feature that runs tasks on Your behalf. Such
a task can create, modify and delete files, run commands, and operate a web
browser. You choose whether to start one, what to ask it to do, and how much
latitude to give it.

You are responsible for the consequences of any task You start. Do not give an
autonomous task access to anything You are not prepared to see changed or lost.


6. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES
OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, ACCURACY, AND
NON-INFRINGEMENT.

Licensor does not warrant that the Software will be uninterrupted, error-free,
or that its output will be correct. The Software relies on artificial
intelligence models that can be wrong, and its guidance should be treated as a
suggestion to be checked rather than an instruction to be followed.

Nothing in this Agreement excludes or limits any liability that cannot lawfully
be excluded or limited, including liability for death or personal injury caused
by negligence, or for fraud.


7. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, LICENSOR SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY
INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR ANY
LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, GOODWILL OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, ARISING OUT
OF OR RELATING TO THIS AGREEMENT OR THE SOFTWARE, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT OR
OTHERWISE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, LICENSOR'S TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY
ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THIS AGREEMENT OR THE SOFTWARE SHALL NOT EXCEED
THE GREATER OF (a) THE AMOUNT YOU PAID LICENSOR FOR THE SOFTWARE IN THE TWELVE
MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM AROSE, OR (b) FIFTY UNITED STATES DOLLARS (USD 50).


8. PRIVACY

The Software's handling of personal data is described in PRIVACY.md, which
accompanies the Software and forms part of this Agreement.


9. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Software includes components licensed by others, listed in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Those components are governed by their own licences,
which take precedence over this Agreement in respect of those components.


10. UPDATES

The Software can download and install its own updates. An update is governed by
this Agreement unless it is accompanied by different terms. You may turn
automatic updates off in the Software's settings.


11. TERMINATION

This licence ends automatically if You breach it. On termination You must stop
using the Software and remove it from Your computers. Sections 4, 5, 6, 7 and
12 survive termination.


12. GENERAL

If any provision of this Agreement is held unenforceable, the rest remains in
force. Licensor's failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver of it. This
Agreement is the entire agreement between You and Licensor about the Software.

The governing law and the courts that will hear any dispute are to be inserted
before this Agreement is used, and should be those of the place where Licensor
is established.


